{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529062-w5-remix-of-rules-and-settings","id":1529062,"title":"W5 remix of rules and settings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-20T20:37:05-08:00","id":1529062,"title":"W5 remix of rules and settings","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> A little over a month ago I started critiquing W5 and thinking of an alternate setting and rules that made sense in a general World Of Darkness 5th Edition context. I ended up making a 33 page document of both critique of W5 and an entirely different setting and rule system. While not complete, it's complete enough to share.<br /> <br /> I present a pdf draft of the <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ec258PrLWeU0F-Yy6tUy6lmkTVtX7Rud/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf Punk Remix</a><br /> <br /> Overall, this new version has a true &quot;crypto-apocalypse&quot; which allows both access to and dismissal of older editions, Auspice is mechanically important, Rage mechanics more defined, there's no &quot;loosing the wolf,&quot; Tenets are mechanically and thematically important and tied to Renown, eliminating the need for the Harano Haglusk (however you spell it) system, Pack cohesion is encouraged mechanically, the spirit world is accessible and useful, this version of the Cult is shown to be fascist without having to be told that it's fascist, and while the setting is bleak and desperate, it's not at all nihilistic.<br /> <br /> I still need to make a pack spirit creation system ; so far, they are connected to shared pack Convictions and Gifts, and have a background for them but don't know what they would do.<br /> <br /> I also need to find a system for creating Gifts. I have them on a 1-5 scale tied to Renown, and drew mostly from Vampire Disciplines because I felt I could trust their balance. Boon/Gift distribution is a uneven as I assigned them more thematically than mechanically.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I need a magical item creation and ranking system, so when players buy them in backgrounds they know the boundaries of what they can ask for.<br /> <br /> I'm looking through another thread on this forum about Caern systems to see if it can help with a more robust system here.<br /> <br /> I also very much need help with systems for exhaustion, hunger, thirst, and dealing with environmental hazards - you can travel the spirit world as long as you want but can't eat or drink anything and its full of dangers, including weather, and to get somewhere might take days. But I don't know any 5th edition systems for dealing with storms or extreme temperature.<br /> <br /> This new setting is more explicitly post-apocalyptic: the characters are part a werewolf generation less than a decade old, with the only connection to the prior werewolf culture are some spirits, and the ruins of the Caerns. I put in a bunch of evidence of what could've happened to the old werewolves to hopefully give a framework for a storyteller, but I don't think enough. My mind's also been blank on possible Lore Sheets.<br /> <br /> If you have ideas with how to solve some the things I need work on above, please share!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28316-pjpaglen","name":"pjpaglen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T20:38:22-08:00","id":1529063,"title":"","content":"While I do like w5 a great deal, I'm looking forward to see what you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T21:40:27-08:00","id":1529067,"title":"","content":"This is good stuff.<br /> <br /> For one, by having the previous generation of garou gone and the slate clean, you offer much more freedom to the players to decide what to be. By having the older setting be a mystery these werewolves have to solve it doesn't denonize what used to be by focuses on reclaiming the old ways.<br /> <br /> Second, auspice matters once more.<br /> <br /> Third, the Worthy are much better antagonists than the CoF. There is no vagueness in how they are worse, they ARE clearly worse by their mentality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T22:08:32-08:00","id":1529069,"title":"","content":"Wow, this is really, really good. I love how it's not only bolder than what we got with the canon W5 (wiping the slate completely clean is probably the best way to handle a true post-apocalyptic situation), but unlike that W5, it still shows respect towards what came before and doesn't feel like it's spitting on long-time fans. The vagueness here actually makes sense and is done in a way that leaves a lot of room for plot threads about finding out what happened and where the werewolves can go from here, actually respecting the players' time and energy. These new Garou are not shamed for their willingness to Act and their goals are explicitly about what ways they try to make the most of the world they've inherited, and that's so refreshing in the face of W5's general dismissal. And making the Worthy pull from the actual problems the old Garou had instead of just being a proxy for a developer's grudge (looks like they take just as much from the Red Talons lol) means they actually make a lot of sense here as antagonists.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I'm not much of a mechanics person, especially with 5e, so I can't help with many of those questions. But I definitely encourage you to keep up the good work, because this is amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T22:13:02-08:00","id":1529070,"title":"","content":"Also:<br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1440_1705817499805_58\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1440\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1440\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1440&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> I find this little easter egg (Bat being redeemed) absolutely delightful. It's a treat for those who know the lore, and even if you don't I love how it serves as a subtle little hint that things can be dragged back from the brink.<br /> <br /> (Sorry for the double post, I don't want to trigger the editing glitch)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T18:52:36-08:00","id":1529122,"title":"","content":"thanks, Ana and Ghost-fox.<br /> <br /> Is there anything else from older editions that would make good &quot;set-props&quot; that would help a storyteller weave an apocalypse mystery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28316-pjpaglen","name":"pjpaglen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T01:48:53-08:00","id":1529146,"title":"","content":"I like it, its further away from WtA than W5 in some ways but it absolutely retains the spirit and heart of the game in a way that W5 doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T19:51:16-08:00","id":1529192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pjpaglen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529062-w5-remix-of-rules-and-settings?p=1529122#post1529122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thanks, Ana and Ghost-fox.<br /> <br /> Is there anything else from older editions that would make good &quot;set-props&quot; that would help a storyteller weave an apocalypse mystery?</div> </div> </div> </div>So the original run of WtA did have a sourcebook that takes place during the Apocalypse, in which four scenarios are given for what the endgame for the Garou looks like. While most of these are way, waaaay too tied up in a lot of metaplot business to be useful to translate directly into this project, and some leave the world too scarred to work in this scenario, reading <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Apocalypse_(book)\" target=\"_blank\">the summary over on the wiki</a> might give you some ideas to branch off of as to what could have happened to the original Garou, and ideas for breadcrumbs to lead to whatever conclusion you do end up making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T13:34:32-08:00","id":1532297,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone.<br /> <br /> I updated my punk redux further: I cleaned up the writing and format a bit, added rules for environmental hazards, cleaned up the Boon (gifts) distribution, and provided a framework for a Boon creation. <br /> <br /> Here is <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1o2Diio3utgSkbMMLnsPwDxO-mX8gjxg-/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Version 0.2 of the Punk Remix</a>. <br /> <br /> I'm still figuring out systems for a magical item Background, and a Tutelary (Spirit Patron) background system, and deciding if it really needs one at all. I ended up deciding Den as a background needed no more detail.<br /> <br /> Enjoy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28316-pjpaglen","name":"pjpaglen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T19:20:13-08:00","id":1532308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pjpaglen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529062-w5-remix-of-rules-and-settings#post1529062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone,<br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Op If you want more inspiration for Post apoc WTA setting then you should read this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolf: The Post-Apocalypse<br /> <br /> The Wyrm has won. Gaia is dead. The Weaver is crippled, broken, lobotomized. The Wyld, diminished and corrupted but forever untamed, spews forth an endless river of horrors that even the Wyrm finds grotesque. The Wyrm sits atop the charred husk of the world, lord of all, and yet its victory is pyrrhic. It cannot escape its bonds. It can only stew in its pain and self-loathing. With no other enemies to fight, it turns upon itself. And beneath the Wyrm's notice, life clings and fights for its existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Top of the World.<br /> At the Top of the World sits the Wyrm in all its terrible glory. Its three heads rise up so high that they're visible from all points in the Northern Hemisphere. They constantly bite and tear at each other. None can slay the others, but they all try. As a result, they're covered with wounds that drip foul ichor and where that ichor touches the ground spawn great and terrible Banes. Seasons are no longer determined by the movements of the Earth, but by which of the Heads is dominant.<br /> <br /> The Season of Calamity is also the Season of Growth. It is when farmers plant their corps, and when their crops try to kill them. It is the time when the sky battles the ground, when the wind fights the rain, when trees uproot themselves and turn to slaughter, not that there are many trees left.<br /> <br /> The Season of Consumption is the Season of Harvest, of Glutony, of Famine, of Cannibalism. It is the season when It is the season when parents eat their children not because they are hungry, but merely for the pleasure of the eating. It is the season when the sun shines less, or not at all, it's light eaten before reaching the earth.<br /> <br /> The Season of Corruption is thankfully rare.<br /> <br /> <br /> Motorwolves and Chromebears:<br /> To the very end, Gaia loved her children and it is only natural for children to outlive their parents. Knowing that she was doomed, Gaia made a choice to give her children a chance at the cost of the little life she had left. At the moment the Wyrm manifested on Earth, every living creature on Earth's surface experienced the First Change. Not a drop of changing blood was required, as Gaia was giving her very essence to her children. Extinct breeds walked the earth for the first time since the War of Rage. New breeds never before imagined came into being. Confused and without any sort of leadership or guidance the new Fera were immediately crushed. Most died. Some survived.<br /> <br /> The survivors built new tribes for themselves, made new societies from the ruins of the old. Some crowd around the last fading cairns, hoping that the remnants of Gaia's life force will somehow protect them. Others find safety and power in mobility. They prowl the roads as normads and fight for control of the world's last remaining stores of oil. Elders and Wise Ones talk of a road warrior named Max, a myth from the before time.<br /> <br /> You are a part of a Motorpack. Inspired by the legends of the World Before, you strive to make the Wasteland better than it is, so that others can eek out their livings just a little easier.<br /> <br /> A Non-Exhaustive List of Locations:<br /> The Wyrmlands - Area closest to the Wyrm's domain at the North Pole, where banes constantly war with each other. The Wyrmlands are defined by massive lakes of Wyrmblood fed by the Wyrm's dripping wounds.<br /> The Motorlands - The Wastelands of North America, dominated by nomadic motorpacks. Being so close to the Wyrmlands, the Motorlands suffer from the worst of both worlds, both spiritual monstrosities and personal callousness. The Motorlands' inhabitants find it difficult to accept the possibility of hope, and are in desperate need of legends.<br /> The Ant Empires - South America's rainforsts, still living in spite of the Wyrm's efforts, are dominated by militaristic wereant hives.<br /> The Down Under - Australia, too far away from the Wyrm's emergence point and not important enough to bother with got off relatively unscathed, except for the complete collapse of human civilization. Major cities, unable to feed themselves due to infrastructure collapse, have been abandoned and reclaimed by what is left of nature. </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure it's vastly different from you're pitch due to the fact it's intend to be the same setting as WTA and nearly every human and most of the animals are converted into shape shifter but you could take some inspiration for you're setting..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 03-09-2024, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}